The new online consultation service for students, researchers, and staff at research and collection institutions on all aspects of research data management will launch on March 17, 2026, from 9:00 to 10:00 a.m. online via Zoom.

Going forward, experts from the humanities NFDI consortia NFDI4Memory, NFDI4Culture, NFDI4Objects, and Text+ will be available once a month to answer your questions on all topics related to research data management. If needed, individual discussions can be continued in breakout rooms. 


The Schedule can be found [here](https://www.nfdi.de/humanitiesnfdi/).

Zoom: (https://uni-goettingen.zoom-x.de/j/67331197843?pwd=84wTp1UjPbjtvGpOUaNyHpWmk4ny8C.1)


Urgent questions?


No problem: The Humantinies@NFDI helpdesks are available at any time:   


NFDI4Culture: [Helpdesk](https://nfdi4culture.de/de/helpdesk.html)     


NFDI4Memory: [Helpdesk](https://4memory.de/unterstuetzung/offene-sprechstunde)


NFDI4Objects: [Helpdesk](https://www.nfdi4objects.net/portal/helpdesk/)   


Text+: [Helpdesk](https://text-plus.org/helpdesk/)


Registration is not required.